Z||000005||1FST2M6||02-16-2000||09:39 PM||||Yes it is a fire extinguisher.. an ABC. It was out of its braackets at the time the photo was taken.. the actual bracket is mounted where the parking brake used to be. Got the whole thing bracket and 3# bottle from NAPA for $25. The Harness is VERY comfy so are the seats but a REAL pain evertime i get in and out of them.. and they are about 2.5" lower than the factory seats. Set at a 17* tilt heir perfect for hard driving and even harder cornering and stopping. the lower thigh support keeps you planted in the seat when your DEEP on the binders. Oh as for the Helmet ? no not around town but at the track I have to cause it according to NHRA rules (even on friday night test and tune) if your car runs 13.5 or faster you must wear a helmet. <p>[This message has been edited by 1FST2M6 (edited 02-16-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000006||FIEROCIOUS||02-17-2000||04:20 AM||||Those look good man!<BR>I've got a pair of RCI raceing seats in mine!<BR>They suck though! Bad pain in the middle of the back when pushing hard on the brakes. With the frame I made they sit 1/2 inch higher than stock I only use them for big race events.<BR>Are yours comffy?<BR>How did you mount them?<BR>Did you drill holes in the floor?<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000007||1FST2M6||02-17-2000||08:42 AM||||yes their comfy! but a pain to get in to.. Their pirelli webed and aren't like the older Clubmans with the springs in the back. they look sharp and do thier job well. I bought the Corbeau seat tracks custom fit to my car... thier $60 each. VERY smooth operating and anodized blue! ||||reg||1
Z||000008||Shaun41178||02-17-2000||11:10 PM||||I wanted to get the Corbeau Forzas.  You told me that they wouldn't fit.  In what area don't they fit?  Actually the seats you have look like the Forza I wanted to get.  How much were they a piece?  I only plan on getting one.  The Forza is $220 last time I checked.  You said that is the Clubman that you bought?  They must have changed the style?<P>The only bad thing about me getting a racing seat is losing the rear speakers as mine are in the seats.||||reg||1
Z||000009||stsmithgt||02-19-2000||02:32 PM||||Back in the earlier 70's, there was a car that had a set of seat tracks on the drivers side that would rotate. Bonneville? 442? Riviera?  I can't remember-  head hurting-- need to stop thinking. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> It seems like that would help subdue the problem of getting in and out.  I suppose they could be modified to fit.||||reg||1
Z||000010||Monkeyman||02-19-2000||07:05 PM||||The Cutlass was one of them, but I don't think there's enough room in a Fiero to rotate the seats.  One of my ex-wives (I've got 2 of them) had a Cutlass with the turntable seats.  There was barely enough room in that.||||reg||1
